    "body": "# Description\n\nSix `RuntimeError` messages in the fusible-op API build one string from four fragments and leave the `f` off the first one, so the brace expression that names the offending subclass goes out verbatim:\n\n```\n{self.__class__.__name__} operation has 1 extra tensor inputs and 0 extra tensor outputs.\nIt should override `fuser_forward` instead of `op_forward`.\n```\n\nThe two fragments after it are f-strings and do interpolate, so the counts are right and only the class name is lost, which is the one part a caller cannot work out for themselves. These are the guards that fire when a subclass declares extra tensor inputs or outputs and implements `op_forward` / `op_backward` instead of `fuser_forward` / `fuser_backward`, so the message exists to say which operation got it wrong.\n\nThe same four-fragment message appears six more times in the same tree with the `f` in place, in `basic/swiglu.py:499`, `:507`, `basic/activation.py:383`, `:391`, `basic/grouped_linear.py:852` and `:860`. These six were the ones that were missed.\n\nDemonstrated standalone, since it is a property of the language rather than of TE:\n\n```python\nclass Demo:\n    num_extra_inputs = 1\n    num_extra_outputs = 0\n\n    def msg(self):\n        return (\n            \"{self.__class__.__name__} operation has \"\n            f\"{self.num_extra_inputs} extra tensor inputs \"\n            f\"and {self.num_extra_outputs} extra tensor outputs. \"\n            \"It should override `fuser_forward` instead of `op_forward`.\"\n        )\n\n\nprint(Demo().msg())\n```\n\n```\n{self.__class__.__name__} operation has 1 extra tensor inputs and 0 extra tensor outputs. It should override `fuser_forward` instead of `op_forward`.\n```\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\n\n## Changes\n\n- `transformer_engine/pytorch/ops/op.py:724`, `:759` — `BasicOperation.fuser_forward` / `fuser_backward` guards.\n- `transformer_engine/pytorch/ops/basic/add_extra_input.py:47`, `:55`.\n- `transformer_engine/pytorch/ops/basic/make_extra_output.py:52`, `:60`.\n\nOne character each, nothing else touched.\n\n# Checklist:\n\n- [x] I have read and followed the [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.rst)\n- [x] The functionality is complete\n- [x] I have commented my code, particularly in hard-to-understand areas\n- [x] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\n- [ ] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works\n- [ ] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes\n\nNo test, and I would rather say so than claim otherwise. Reaching these lines needs a built extension plus a custom `BasicOperation` subclass that declares extra tensor inputs or outputs and implements `op_forward` instead of `fuser_forward`, and nothing in the tree asserts on this text today. I have no GPU and no built extension here.\n\nWhat I did run: `black 24.4.2 --line-length=100 --preview --enable-unstable-feature=string_processing`, the exact arguments from `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, reports all three files unchanged, and `pylint 3.3.1 --rcfile=pylintrc` rates `add_extra_input.py` and `make_extra_output.py` 10.00/10. On `op.py` pylint reports `E0611: No name 'common' in module 'transformer_engine'`, which is the unbuilt extension on this machine and not related to the change.\n",
