      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=78516394\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n**[Low impact]** This PR appears safe to merge; it fixes the class names in existing error messages.\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nFixes six `RuntimeError` messages so they show the operation’s class name instead of `{self.__class__.__name__}`.\n- Fusible-operation errors now name the operation class.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"\\[PyTorch\\] Interpolate the class name in ...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/4f0588b922fd6eddb70547cdc4687ad5efae5c85) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_expert&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=code_reviews&utm_content=nvidia/transformerengine)</sub>",
